list : list is a collection of multiple values stored in a single variable
ex: 
marks=[30,40,50,60]

a list can store string , integer, float , boolean all together  

LIST SLICING:  list slicing means it is used to get a part of a list 
syntax: list[start:end]

ex: 
marks=[80,30,49,46,46,46]
print(marks[1:4])

ex2: 
marks=[80,30,49,46,46,46]
print(marks[-3:-1])



LIST METHODS
suppose nums=[2,1,3]


1 APPEND() : it adds the element at the end 
ex : 
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.append(4)
print(nums)


2.SORT() : it will sorts in assending order (small to big)
ex: 
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.sort()
print(nums)

3.SORT(REVERSE=TRUE) : sorts in dessending order 
ex:
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.sort(reverse=True)
print(nums)


4.REVERSE()  : it reverse the current order
ex:
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.reverse()
print(nums)

5.REMOVE():  it removes the value
ex: 
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.remove(1)
print(nums)


6.POP() : it used to remove the element at the index
ex: 
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.pop(1)
print(nums)


7.INSERT(): it insert the values at specific index's position
ex: 
nums=[2,1,3]
nums.insert(1,5)
print(nums)
